            <td class="py-2.5 px-3">Very high risk of chronic morbidity</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- BMI Differences by Gender & Age -->
    <h3>3. Understanding BMI Differences in Men, Women & by Age</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>BMI for Women:</strong> Women naturally possess higher essential body
        fat (approximately <strong>21% – 33%</strong>) than men due to
        reproductive physiology and hormonal differences. While a woman and a
        man of the same height and weight have the identical BMI score, the
        female body composition reflects a higher body fat percentage and lower
        lean muscle mass.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>BMI for Men:</strong> Men generally carry higher bone density and
        muscle mass with lower essential body fat (approximately <strong
          >8% – 20%</strong
        >). Highly muscular men may register in the "overweight" BMI range
        despite having low body fat.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>BMI by Age (Seniors 60+):</strong> In elderly adults, a slightly higher
        BMI range of <strong>22.0 to 27.0 kg/m²</strong> is associated with lower
        mortality, providing nutritional reserves and protection against bone mineral
        loss (osteoporosis).
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>BMI for Children & Teens (2 to 19 Years):</strong> Standard adult
        BMI cutoffs do not apply to children. Pediatricians utilize <strong
          >CDC BMI-for-Age Growth Charts</strong
        > where BMI is interpreted as a percentile relative to peers of the same age
        and sex.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Why Use Our Calculator -->
    <h3>4. Key Features of Our Free Online BMI Calculator</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Visual Radial Speedometer:</strong> Interactive semi-circular gauge
        clearly illustrating your exact BMI position with a dynamic pointer.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Dual Unit Support:</strong> Seamlessly input values in Metric (kg,
