      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Gender-Specific Health Insights:</strong> Calculates estimated Body
        Fat % (Deurenberg formula), Ideal Body Weight (Devine formula), and Basal
        Metabolic Rate (BMR) for both men and women.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Submit on Demand:</strong> Clean, uncluttered interface that only
        generates results when you click Calculate.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Asian vs Global Reference:</strong> Toggle between WHO Global and
        Asian/Indian health benchmarks.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div
      class="not-prose mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-blue-100 bg-blue-50/70 p-5 text-sm text-slate-700 dark:border-blue-900/50 dark:bg-blue-950/25 dark:text-slate-200"
    >
      <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">
        BMI is a screening tool, not a diagnosis
      </h3>
      <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">
        BMI is useful for a quick height-and-weight check, but it does not
        directly measure body fat, muscle mass, pregnancy status or individual
        medical risk. Speak with a qualified healthcare professional for
        personalised guidance, especially for children, pregnancy, eating
        concerns or ongoing health conditions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h3>5. BMI references and next steps</h3>
    <p>
      This calculator uses the standard adult BMI formula and shows WHO-style
      categories for adults. For a child or teenager aged 2 to 19, use a <strong
        >BMI-for-age percentile</strong
      > tool rather than adult cutoffs. You can review the underlying guidance from
      the <a
        href="https://www.cdc.gov/growth-chart-training/hcp/using-bmi/calculating-bmi.html"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">CDC BMI calculation guide</a
      > and the <a
        href="https://www.who.int/europe/news-room/fact-sheets/item/nutrition---maintaining-a-healthy-lifestyle"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">WHO healthy-weight reference</a
      >.
    </p>
